  "description": "Months (1-12) in which fruit, nuts and vegetables are available from Slovenian production. 'harvest' = fresh domestic supply (the source's 'obdobje ponudbe' / 'obdobje z močno ponudbo' bands for crops that are not stored); 'storage' = Slovenian crop sold from storage (cold-stored crops marked (H) in the source, stored apples, pears and nuts). Items with domestic=false are imported only. Items not listed are not covered by the source (no data), not necessarily imported.",
  "source": "Transcribed from the seasonal calendars of the Ministry of Agriculture's 'Naša super hrana' portal: Tabela 1-3 'Sezonski koledar' (vegetables, fruit, apples) in the article 'Jesenska svežina', supplemented by the chart 'Dostopnost slovenskega sadja skozi leto' (peach, plum, redcurrant, apple and pear storage). Where the two charts disagree, the fresh months are their union. The harvest/storage split for stored crops is a FoodMission interpretation, as is main-crop potato beyond the source's early-potato row. The import-only list was added by FoodMission. No open licence: the portal's terms state that all content is the property of the Ministry of Agriculture and is protected by copyright.",
